# No em dashes anywhere on AI Glimpse

The user has explicitly banned em dashes (`—`, U+2014) from this project. This applies to:

- All HTML page copy and headings
- Article body content (so all Claude rewriting prompts must enforce this)
- README, SETUP-GUIDE, comments, commit messages
- Logos, taglines, brand language
- Any new code, prose, or generated content

## Replace em dashes with:

- **Comma** for parenthetical / soft pause: `OpenAI ships GPT-5 Turbo, claims 40% gain`
- **Period** for hard break / new thought: `Fresh AI news. Every 30 minutes.`
- **Colon** for label / introduction: `The pipeline: fetch, dedupe, publish.`
- **Parentheses** for asides: `(the lab\'s latest round)`
- **Hyphen** only for compound words: `state-of-the-art`, never as a sentence separator

## Examples

❌ `The new model debuts with a 2M-token context — putting fresh pressure on Anthropic.`
✅ `The new model debuts with a 2M-token context, putting fresh pressure on Anthropic.`

❌ `Your daily glimpse into AI — premium reporting, every morning.`
✅ `Your daily glimpse into AI. Premium reporting, every morning.`

## Enforcement in the pipeline

When updating `scripts/fetch-and-publish.mjs`, the Claude rewrite prompt MUST include an instruction forbidding em dashes in `body_html`, `title`, `subtitle`, and `meta_description`. After Claude returns, also do a programmatic `.replace(/—/g, ',')` (or context-appropriate replacement) as a safety net.

## En dashes (`–`, U+2013)

Also avoid. Use a hyphen or a word like "to" instead: `2024 to 2026`, not `2024–2026`.
